If a person has a cardiac arrest, breathing is gone, the heartbeat is gone, and there is no role in the strangulation of people.
It is necessary to do artificial breathing and chest compressions to save people.
I found that very few people now have this kind of awareness to learn first aid, but when it happens, it’s too late, so we’re calling on everyone to learn this skill so that we can react in time in the face of an unexpected situation.
