First of all, I personally believe that "Four Seas" is an all-round film, in a variety of senses.
But you have to say that this film is not a highlight or not, and that is not at least the soundtrack selection is very good.
There are many kinds of rotten pieces, so that you can fall asleep in the cinema, so that after reading it, it is a kind of indignation, "Four Seas" for the audience is like a monkey on Emei Mountain, it can ignite your anger in countless ways.
In terms of insulting the audience at this point, Han Han is really talented.
The most painful thing in this film is that it seems to be a creature in a gram novel, indescribable, and many loopholes are like a windbreaker on the body of Little Marco.
Even after reading it, you will doubt whether there is any metaphor implied by the director, but when you think carefully, you find that it is actually a piece of shit.
Let’s start with something that’s very difficult for me to understand.
The man's residence should be on a small island in the south, depending with his grandmother.
Her grandmother had a desire to see the snow, and then the plot arranged for a gentleman in the neighborhood to drive her to the northeast to see the snow.
Elderly people sit in the van from the south to the northeast to see the snow?
He and his father were very relieved about this.
And then the old man didn’t come down.
Open a hotel on an abandoned ship, how does the female brother get a business license?
Why is it easy to close a section of the mountain road?
Then the truck that sent steel bars in the middle of the road was parked on the side of the road, and even the truck driver could not find it.
The feeling of this tool is also very obvious.
Why does a small mixed car party who does not have credit and is suspected of illegality become an auxiliary police officer?
In the face of usury, why don't you call the police, the police in the film also asked whether there are any difficulties?
An adult knows how to use a smartphone, but he does not know how to open the door with a room card in the hotel, and then forcibly arranges not to find the hotel owner, sitting outside the door of the room to sleep for a night?
This inexplicable plot pervades the whole film, and it hurts me because it’s so outrageous that I remember them.
In addition to the plot, what is worse is the main theme of the film, or that this film has no theme at all, which is an abominable suture.
At the beginning of the film you will think that he wants to make a comedy, more than 20 minutes later you guessed that it may be an inspirational film, you think it may be a drama that wants to reflect the survival of young people in a small town, after watching it, you don't know exactly what you saw, followed by deep doubts about yourself.
For most people is actually very familiar with all kinds of movies, such as if you want to shoot a motorcyclist, then motivation + comedy and then tell the audience how a talented rookie step by step to achieve success.
If you want to make love movies, then you honestly talk about the entanglement between the small town youth and the waiter sister who likes to ride motorcycles.
If you want to reflect reality, then at the very least your plot can't appear contrary to the normal world.
(For example, Yin Zheng’s new motorcycle has just been burned, and then he can still sing), he can’t open some brain holes that even Kennedy couldn’t see.)
As far as the hostess are obviously not mentally retarded and can behave in some ways, like a five-year-old child, I really don't know whether this is the cause of acting or the director's request.
There is also a point that I don't want to understand why Han Han, as a racing driver, is so keen to add a crash plot in his own movies?
This kind of film is arranged in the Spring Festival file, is it for the audience to plug?
