Chongqing middle vocational school pilot modern apprenticeship enrollment is the enterprise associate staff-Xinhua.com
Yesterday, the reporter learned from the Municipal Education Commission that from this year, the city will pilot the "modern apprenticeship" talent training model in 60 secondary vocational schools, and the students who receive the pilot training will also have apprenticeship status, and will be pre-recorded as unit employees by the pilot enterprises after enrollment.
The Municipal Education Commission requires the standardization of secondary vocational school enrollment and enterprise employment procedures, clear the dual status of middle school students and enterprise prospective employees of apprentices, in accordance with the principle of two-way selection, apprentices, schools and enterprises signed a tripartite agreement, for apprentices who have reached the age of 16 and not reached the age of 18, they must be signed by apprentices, guardians, schools and enterprises, to determine the rights and interests of all parties and the specific positions, teaching content, protection of rights and interests.
The pilot schools are encouraged to adopt the form of modern apprenticeships and cooperate with enterprises to jointly carry out pre-job training and transfer training for enterprise employees.
The pilot schools should reform the talent training model.
Schools and enterprises jointly design talent training programs, and jointly formulate professional teaching standards, curriculum standards, job standards, enterprise teacher standards, quality control standards and corresponding implementation plans.
The pilot is based on the training system as a pilot cycle, and the internship time of the students in the enterprise is determined according to the professional personnel training program, and the internship is generally 6 months.
In the enterprise practice should implement the enterprise group management model, according to the characteristics of different majors, a teacher can bring 2 to 5 apprentices to form a learning group, to ensure that students are proficient in the skills required for each rotating position.
According to the arrangement, from 2016 to August 2019, the city identified 60 city-level modern apprenticeship pilots in three batches, each with a pilot number of about 50 people, training a total of about 3,000 students (apprentices).
In accordance with the principle of first-to-proverse, from point-to-face to gradual advancement, we will explore the establishment of a long-term mechanism for joint enrollment, joint training, and integrated education of schools and enterprises, effectively improve students' job skills, and improve the employment rate and employment quality of students' counterparts.
