The China Children's Center will hold a series of activities to let the children "high-tech" through the "June 1" - Xinhua.com
BEIJING, May 20 (Xinhua) -- Reporters learned from the China Children's Center on the 20th that before and after the "June 1" Children's Day from May 28 to June 1, the China Children's Center plans to hold a series of activities such as children's maker experience, children's visual arts festival, and parent-child book carnival, so that children can spend "June 1" in the charm of cutting-edge science and technology.
It is understood that the activities held by the China Children's Center during this year's "June 1st" Children's Day, including the "Aijia Creative Cool" children's future learning carnival, the first children's visual arts festival, the "Shoke Carnival" activities, and a series of activities such as "The whole family loves to read" picture books.
Li Zhongming, deputy director of the China Children's Center, introduced at the 2016 "June 1st" Children's Day media briefing held on the 20th, saying that the future learning carnival of "Aijia Creative Cool" children is the key activity of this year's China Children's Center to celebrate "June 1).
The event focuses on the organic combination of social innovation and the personal creativity of the family, through the participation of children and families to experience a variety of innovative educational activities, so that innovative practices can become the cultural genes of public families, so that "hands-on" will become a new learning and lifestyle for the majority of families.
It is reported that the "Aijia Creative Cool" children's future learning carnival includes dozens of cutting-edge scientific and technological experiences such as "bean fruit maker" experience activities, the anniversary celebration of the old cattle children's exploration museum and "exploring the whole family's love 童萋萌 on June 1" activities, the VR national experience plan, and the interactive workshop of the "maker tribe".
