Jiangxi will train 10,000 rural primary school sound and beauty teachers in three years - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Nanchang, May 22 (Reporter Chen Yushan) The reporter recently learned from the Jiangxi Provincial Department of Education that in order to enhance the capacity of teachers in scarce disciplines and realize the balanced development of compulsory education in rural areas, since 2016, Jiangxi Province has planned to use three years for the province's villages (townships and below) to train qualified music, fine arts, and physical education teachers for each primary school, a total of 10,000.
It is understood that this training is aimed at Jiangxi rural primary schools under the age of 45 with music, fine arts, sports knowledge base or talent, can also serve as music, art, physical education courses of other discipline teachers.
Through training, they can master the basic knowledge and teaching skills of the teaching of sound and aesthetic disciplines, update teaching ideas and concepts, master modern teaching methods, improve discipline teaching ability, activity design ability, campus cultural ability and self-development ability, and build a team of multi-skilled sound and aesthetic teachers to alleviate the lack of teachers in rural sound and physical beauty.
In order to ensure the quality and effectiveness of training, Jiangxi is also planned to train one of the province's 100 counties (cities, districts) primary school music, fine arts, and sports, a total of 300 trainers, and comprehensively improve their teaching and demonstration leading capabilities, teaching and research activities design organization capabilities, training capabilities, and network training workshop construction capabilities, and play a teaching, demonstration, guidance and supervision role.
