The 18th World Beverage Innovation Awards are co-organized by FoodBev Media with Brau Beviale in Nuremberg, Germany.
It has attracted 279 entries from 25 countries and 22 different categories.
On October 15th, the list of finalists will be announced, and the list of final winners will be announced online on November 11.
We have seen that the LP28 sugar-free yoghurt of Yuanyuan Forest was shortlisted for the best milk beverage award, Yili's "GOGO Wuhan" marketing was shortlisted for the best marketing activities, and the packaging of Pepsi and People's Daily new media cooperation was also shortlisted for the best packaging design/label award.
Laura Nettle, senior marketing director at FoodBev Media, said: “We are delighted to celebrate the 18th anniversary of the World Beverage Innovation Awards with Brau Beviale.
From new tastes, new concepts and new features to branding, packaging, and manufacturing, as the industry continues to innovate in a more sustainable way, we’re seeing trends in the beverage industry.
The World Beverage Innovation Award recognizes new and ambitious new products and developments for new and old brands in the global beverage industry this year.
Here’s a full list of finalists in each category.
The technology developed by Ardagh Group can re-melt 100% of the recycled glass into new bottles.
The box is 100% recyclable, which can reduce packaging by 66% and reduce carbon emissions by 97%.
LatCub is 100% biodegradable, uses less paper, and does not use environmentally harmful glue or tape.
The technology developed by Ardagh Group can remelt 100% of the recycled glass into new bottles.
The final list of winners will be announced on FoodBev Media’s YouTube channel on November 11 (British Daylight Savings Time), and FBIF will continue to report for you, please look forward to it!
