Xinhua all-media + 丨 Beijing Youth Ice Hockey League to fuel the enthusiasm of the Winter Olympics - Xinhua.com
On December 11st, Beijing Dream ING team player Pang Yaotian (middle) shot in the game.
On the same day, in the 2021-2022 season, the Beijing Youth Ice Hockey Club League continued to compete in the major ice rinks in Beijing.
The league is divided into the regular season and the playoffs, and the age of the participating athletes is U6 to U18, and the group is divided into competitive groups and selection groups, attracting nearly 3,600 players from 256 teams in the city.
After more than ten years of development, the Beijing Youth Hockey Club League has now become a platform for young ice hockey enthusiasts in Beijing to exchange technology and communicate with friends, as well as conveying excellent players for the Beijing Youth Ice Hockey Team and the youth team.
The league plays the driving role of the event in Beijing's youth ice hockey movement, ignites the enthusiasm of ice hockey in the Winter Olympics, and lays the foundation for the development of ice hockey in Beijing in the post-Winter Olympic period.
The girl as a target for her sister's fundraising: "It's okay to think that it's a skin injury" - Xinhua.com
A girl stands in front of a large wooden board in Hangzhou Wulin Square, with the words "human meat target, ten yuan and one arrow".
Yesterday's morning, a photo of "Hangzhou girl Gandang's 'story target' to raise funds for her sister" blew up the circle of friends.
The photo shows that a girl in Wulin Square in Hangzhou is standing in front of a large plank slightly taller than a person, with the words "human meat target, ten yuan and an arrow" written on the wooden board, indicating that passers-by can use bow and arrow shooting after payment.
This behavior aroused heated discussion among netizens.
Last night, the head of publicity of the Lower City Branch of the Hangzhou Public Security Bureau confirmed to the reporter of the Beijing News that the police confirmed that the girl made such an excessive move by collecting donations for her sister, but this behavior is not worthy of promotion, and after warning, the girl left the local police station yesterday.
The girl's street "strive target" fundraiser was warned
In the online image, a long-haired girl is standing in front of a large wooden board with the words "human meat target, ten yuan and an arrow" written in black ink, and she has her bank account and WeChat and Alipay account on another wooden board in front of her.
This image caused controversy after going online.
Some netizens believe that this move is "eye-catching begging behavior", and many netizens sympathize with it.
â€œWe were patrolling around 10 a.m. on the 23rd to the side of the plaza, and there were already many onlookers.â€
In an interview with local media, the police of Tianshui police station near the incident said that there were a total of two girls in the booth, all of whom were about 20 years old, dressed young and beautiful.
Among them, the girl who is a "human meat target" has been crying, asking passers-by to play this game; the other girl is on the edge to help shout, saying that her friend's sister has leukemia, and now urgently needs surgery costs, please help everyone.
â€œWe got in touch with the local police in Guizhou and learned that the girl was raising funds for her sister's leukemia treatment.â€
Last night, the head of publicity of the Lower City Branch of the Hangzhou Public Security Bureau told the Beijing News reporter that the girl was named Ji Jiali to raise funds for her sister Ji Jiayan.
However, due to the fact that the treatment still needs more than 300,000 costs, it was impossible to think of a good way to raise funds, and this kind of behavior was made.
He said that in the whole process, the two girls were a target, one was responsible for playing hands, but did not participate in it, and in the whole process, there was no archery, but someone onlookers and took photos on Weibo.
Later, the police were identified by the public security department, and the bow and arrows used did not fall within the scope of control.
The person in charge said, "do not advocate the adoption of this kind of eyeball fundraising."
After being alerted by the police at the police station, she left the police station.
