What’s the biggest fire in 2021?
Undoubtedly the Tokyo Olympics.
Do you think that only Olympic athletes can win the award?
Some time ago, there was an article that the project manager can impact the Olympic project of the gold medal is very hot, which mentioned that the project managers are in many projects, it is absolutely possible to take the lead, and no one can afford: moving bricks, traveling for business, staying up late is the daily life of the project manager, saving the fire, carrying the pot, and apologizing are not the same.
What seems to be a joke is an article, but it also shows the daily poignancy of the project managers, and what is behind them is the inability to work on the current project management work.
People who are engaged in project management have gradually chosen to take some actions to get themselves out of the difficulties of their work.
Judging by the number of PMP (Internationally Accredited Project Management Professional Eligimenties), more and more project management practitioners are learning to improve their project management skills.
According to the "China Project Management Twenty Years Development Report (1999-2019)" said that as of September 2019, there were nearly 600,000 cumulative PMP® applicants across the country, about 420,000 people have passed PMP® certification, and the number of valid holders is about 300,000, accounting for 31.2% of the global PMP® license.
In the past 10 years, the number of PMP holders has increased year by year, which shows that more and more project managers are aware that it is no longer advisable to do things by simply copying the "old experiences" of the past, and the rapidly changing working environment allows us to know a way to learn and stand on the shoulders of scientific giants to explore the way forward.
However, can PMP ensure that the project management work is unimpeded?
Many project management beginners said that by learning related courses such as PMP/IPMP, they can systematically grasp the top ten areas of project management and five process groups and other relevant knowledge points, but they are still confused when they really carry out project management work.
Many project managers often feedback the following questions: project management awareness is not in place, relying solely on personal experience, empty project management theory, do not know how to practice; lack of systematic project management process system support, the work can not be landed, project estimation is not accurate, the control sensitivity is poor, the project is delayed; member division of labor is not clear, the team's "old oil bar" does not know how to deal with cross-departmental assistance communication is not smooth, the project is difficult to advance.
Therefore, focusing on product innovation and R&D management for more than ten years, it has helped many outstanding enterprises to train a large number of key R&D talents such as product managers and project managers, and has won the honorary titles of "Chinese enterprise R&D and management talent training demonstration base", with the "R & D project manager training camp" online course.
"R&D project manager training" online course This is an online fragmented way of learning, combined with many R&D-based enterprises practical cases, tools and methods, to help you master the project manager's knowledge and standard actions, on their own project management advanced road.
It’s also an opportunity for companies to use lower costs and fewer inputs to facilitate the training process of project managers and bring efficient operational outcomes for businesses.
Without saying, we can first see how other students evaluate this course: this course is not only by Zhongtian Huaxia expert team (formerly HUAWEI R & D management team), combined with the international advanced project management methodology and many well-known enterprise real business scenarios, the content of the course for in-depth professional explanations.
It will provide scientific and practical management tools and methods, rich template forms, and help trainees to translate the learning content into specific work after class.
