Iran's president: if sanctions are lifted, Iran's nuclear talks are expected to reach an agreement - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Tehran, December 11 (Reporter Gao Wencheng Wang Shoubao) Iranian President Lehi said in the Iranian capital Tehran on the 11th that if the United States lifts sanctions against Iran, the negotiation of a comprehensive agreement on the Iranian nuclear issue can reach a "good agreement".
According to the information released on the website of the Iranian president, Lehi said at a meeting with Iranian envoys to neighboring countries on the same day that through the submission of proposals to other relevant parties to the Iranian nuclear agreement, Iran has proved the sincerity of its own negotiations.
If the U.S. side is determined, "the road to an agreement will be unimpeded."
In April this year, the relevant parties of the Iranian nuclear agreement held talks in Vienna, Austria, to discuss the resumption of compliance between the United States and Iran.
A new round of talks began in Vienna on 29 November, was suspended on December 3 and resumed on the 9th.
