Guangxi college students up to 5 years of entrepreneurship - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Nanning, May 19 (Reporter Zhang Ying) The reporter recently learned from the education department of Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region that in the future, Guangxi colleges and universities will implement a flexible learning system, relax the number of years of college leave, and extend the number of years on the basis of the original academic system, and the time to take a break can be regarded as practical education time.
In order to promote the improvement of college students' entrepreneurship and innovation capabilities, Guangxi education, social security and other departments work together to build an entrepreneurship platform, and build more out-of-school practice teaching bases, university science and technology parks, college students entrepreneurship parks, and entrepreneurship incubation bases to provide external guarantees for college students' entrepreneurship.
According to the requirements, by 2020, the area of innovation and entrepreneurship practice bases in various colleges and universities will reach more than 3,000 square meters for undergraduate schools and more than 2,000 square meters for higher vocational schools.
The government encourages colleges and universities to set up innovation and entrepreneurship credits, giving priority to supporting students with excellent performance in innovation and entrepreneurship practice.
University teachers must go to the industry at least two months every two years, so as to improve the awareness and ability of teachers to innovate entrepreneurship education.
The Education Department of the Autonomous Region requires universities in Guangxi to deeply implement the student innovation and entrepreneurship training program, and strives to enable each college student to participate in an innovation and entrepreneurship training program during the school period.
Universities should actively organize students to participate in all kinds of innovation and entrepreneurship competitions at all levels and provide financial support.
NEWS GOV-MO: The University awards honorary doctorates to seven distinguished individuals
The University of Macau today (11) held the "Emergency and Advanced Degree Award Ceremony in 2021" and awarded honorary doctoral degrees to Liu Zunyi, Chen Kaixian, Nakamura, Li Lanjuan, Li Yiliang, Zhu Lilian and Jiang Chaohui in recognition of their outstanding achievements and significant contributions to the development of society and education.
At the awarding ceremony, Ou Yangyu, Chief Executive and representative of the Superintendent of the Australian University and Director of the Department of Social and Cultural Affairs, was accompanied by Lin Jincheng, Chairman of the Board of Governors of the University of Australia, and Song Yonghua, President of the University of Australia.
Professor Liu Zunyi was awarded the honorary doctorate in education, Professor Chen Kaixian was awarded the honorary doctorate of science, Professor Nakamura was awarded the honorary doctorate of science, Professor Li Lanju was awarded the honorary doctorate in science, Professor Li Yiliang was awarded the honorary doctorate in business administration, Professor Zhu Lilan was awarded the honorary doctorate of science, and Ms. Jiang Chaohui was awarded the honorary doctorate.
In his speech, Ouyang Yu first expressed his warm congratulations to the seven outstanding people who were awarded honorary doctorates, expressed their warm congratulations and high respect, they made extraordinary achievements in different fields and made outstanding contributions to the country's development and the progress of the world; at the same time, Ouyang Yu expressed his most sincere wishes to graduates and parents, and also paid a sincere tribute to the dedicated and academic staff of the university.
Sun Yifeng, a professor at the University of Australia's School of Humanities, said that Professor Liu Zunyi is a world-renowned economist known for his outstanding academic achievements and forward-looking educational concepts.
In addition to achievements in economic development, economic growth and East Asian economy, he is a visionary education leader.
In short, he has made outstanding achievements in many fields.
Sun Yifeng said when he read Nakamura's praise that Professor Nakamura Xiu II is a pioneer of sustainable energy technology.
He became one of the three winners of the 2014 Nobel Prize in Physics for the invention of the blue light-emitting diode (LED).
Professor Nakamura's invention not only completely changed the lighting industry, but also promoted the production of white light-emitting diodes that are now widely used in daily life and industrial production, making great contributions to the well-being of mankind.
Sun Yifeng said when reading Li Lanjuan's praise speech that Professor Li Lanjuan, as a pioneer of China's artificial liver industry, has created a unique and effective Li's artificial liver system to achieve a major breakthrough in the treatment of heavy hepatitis liver failure, significantly reducing the case fatality rate of liver failure.
In this battle against new crown pneumonia, she and her team put forward the "four anti-two balance" scheme and the three major technologies of artificial liver, micro-ecology and stem cells, which significantly improved the treatment rate of serious diseases.
Sun Yifeng said that Professor Li Yiliang laid the foundation for the innovative research of operation management, shaped the way of thinking of supply chain theory and practice, and revolutionized business models around the world.
Li is known for popularizing the concept of long-wheel effects in operational management and has explored measures to deal with this phenomenon.
Nowadays, under the epidemic situation and the tense economic situation, the long whip effect has become more and more prominent, causing serious damage to supply chains.
Li Yiliang's visionary research, such as sending charcoal in the snow, helps the industry cope with difficulties, thus bringing great social value.
Sun Yifeng said that in the scientific research work, she found a breakthrough and innovative dyeing technology for the preparation of samples, and enjoyed a high reputation among domestic and foreign scientific and technological peers.
With extraordinary scientific and technological achievements, she has won important honorary titles such as academicians of the International Eurasian Academy of Sciences, and has won her high status in the world science and technology temple with her brilliant performance.
Chen Xin, acting president of the Greater Chinese Medical Research Institute, said that Professor Chen Kaixian has been engaged in drug research and development for more than 40 years, with outstanding scientific achievements and important contributions to the country, Macao, the University of Macau and the national key laboratories, making him have a high international status and prestige.
His positive role in promoting the development of traditional Chinese medicine in Macao and the Greater Bay Area fully reflects his sense of mission to contribute to the national pharmaceutical development strategy.
The dean of the University of Science and Technology, when reading Jiang Chaohui's praise speech, said that more than 15 major inventions and patents participated in the research and development of Ms. Jiang Chaohui have so far accumulated more than 15 items related to storage virtualization, navigation, file system and power management, all of which are highly practical, widely used, and improve the convenience of human life.
As an accomplished inventor, Ms. Jiang is often able to simplify profound science and technology and theory and popularize the masses.
Finally, Chen Kaixian read the thank-you speech as an honorary doctoral representative.
He is happy to see that the pharmaceutical industry in Macao and the Greater Bay Area has established a good example: from the establishment of the first national key laboratory of Chinese medicine quality research established by the University to the vigorous development of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area, the University has made great contributions to the integration of outstanding talents in the field of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area.
In addition, he believes that the management team of the University has the foresight, not only to provide students with scientific research fertile soil in academia, but also to transport many responsible talents to the society.
He is honored to have exchanges and cooperation with the Australian University and express his sincere congratulations on the achievements of the University in recent years.
