In September 2020, Mr. Lu learned from the housing agent that a factory building in Yuyao Zuting Town, Zhejiang Province, and after looking at the house many times at the scene, Mr. Lu decided to purchase the plant.
In December of the same year, Mr. Lu held consultations on the details of the purchase of the factory and Lin Mou, a family member of the owner of the house, and sent a deposit of 200,000 yuan through a bank transfer on the same day.
Lin in the "factory buying and saying deposit receipt" as the recipient's signature, which states: "If the buyer does not want to buy this plant, this deposit belongs to the seller, if the seller is not willing to sell the plant, the deposit will be doubled back to the seller, the two parties agreed to sign a contract for the sale of the plant within a week."
However, since then, due to the lack of agreement on the terms of major contracts such as the sales scope and payment methods of the plant, the housing sales contract has been delayed.
Considering that the two sides failed to reach a consensus on the content of the contract, a few days later, Lin returned a deposit of 200,000 yuan to Mr. Lu.
It is not easy to look at the house, the deposit is paid, the house is also ready, and the "one foot at the door" signs the contract, and the seller does not sell it, which makes Mr. Lu helpless and angry.
To this end, Mr. Lu sued Lin to the Yuyao Municipal People's Court.
After trial, the court held that the two sides finally failed to sign a formal contract, and could not be attributed only to the defendant, which should be reasonably presumed to have failed for consultation, so the deposit penalty should not be applied in this case, and the defendant did not need to bear the responsibility for the breach of contract of double return of the deposit.
After the first trial, the plaintiff filed an appeal.
Recently, the court of second instance upheld the original judgment.
[Lawyer Reminder] Do the necessary duty of care in the course of the transaction.
At the time of signing the contract, as the buyer, it is necessary for the buyer to do the necessary due diligence obligations, such as verifying the information of the owner of the house, whether the house is occupied and other relevant information, and clarifying the specific time and place of delivery in the contract, so as to prevent disputes between the parties during the performance of the contract.
After Friday's "Democracy Summit", a spokesman for China's Foreign Ministry said in a statement on Saturday (December 11) that the "Leaders' Democracy Summit" held by the United States was "an ideological demarcation, instrumentalization of democracy, weaponization, anti-democracy in the name of democracy, incitement to separatism and confrontation, and shifting domestic contradictions."
"For a long time, the United States has imposed its own political systems and values on others, carried out 'democratic transformation', indiscriminately imposed unilateral sanctions, and instigated a 'color revolution', with disastrous consequences.
'Democracy' has long been the 'weapon of mass destruction' of U.S. intervention in other countries.
This summit is Biden’s move to deliver on his campaign promises.
The two-day meeting took place by video, with leaders from 111 countries around the world invited, including those of Taiwan, but China and Russia were not invited.
On the eve of the summit, China and Russia attacked the United States with problems arising from its own democracy, saying that the United States is not qualified to preside over such a summit.
There have also been questions internationally and in the United States, such as criticizing some leaders who have been invited to participate, such as leaders in the Philippines, Poland and Brazil, who have been invited, and some who have doubted that the Biden administration’s real intention was not to organize the summit for democracy but for geopolitical purposes.
German Chancellor Scholz also participated in the video democracy summit.
China's Foreign Ministry said in a statement on Saturday that "today's American-style democracy is morbid, with money politics, identity politics, political opposition, political polarization, social tearing, racial contradictions, the division between rich and poor, etc."
U.S. President Joe Biden said, "As leaders of government, we have a responsibility to listen to our citizens, strengthen the guardrails of democracy, push for reforms, achieve transparent and accountable governance, are more resilient to authoritarian buffers and shocks, and those who want to pursue power nakedly ahead of the public good."
He stressed that democracy is not taken for granted. "We have to constantly update it in every generation, which, in my view, is the defining challenge of our time."
Biden also said that democracy and human rights around the world "in the face of persistent and worrying challenges, democracy needs to be defended by fighters."
The U.S. side promised a one-year operation after the Democracy Summit, including a $424.4 million initiative to strengthen democracy around the world and provide support to the independent news media.
The United States wants countries to make concrete public commitments to improve their democratic systems ahead of the entity democracy summit planned for the end of 2022.
"Let all of us implement our commitments and report on the progress we've made next year," Biden said.
