Education Information: Beijing Compresses the Proportion of Middle School Admissions in Early 2016 - Xinhua.com
On the 21st and 22nd, Beijing junior high school entrance examination work was carried out by the unified organization of each district education committee.
This year, all districts in Beijing have reduced the proportion of specialty enrollment, and the competition is more intense.
Taking Dongcheng District as an example, this year's proportion of primary and junior high school students in the district does not exceed 5% of the total number of enrollment plans in the district, and the number of planned enrollments is 380, and the proportion of schools does not exceed 10% of the number of school enrollment plans.
All students with sports, arts, science and technology expertise and online registration are eligible to participate in the professional enrollment examination.
In order to facilitate students to participate in the examination nearby, the Dongcheng District continued last year's examination arrangements, setting up 1-2 examination locations in each school district, with a total of 13 inspection sites.
The test points are divided according to the examination area, and the hours are divided into hours, and the students will enter the test site in different examination areas on time on the same day.
On May 23, the list of students passed the online public inspection of the district education entrance examination center, and students can check the results online.
