Qinghai Lake bare carp resources this year increased by 0.71 million tons - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, December 11 (Reporter Luo Xiaofei, Zhang Hongxiang) The reporter learned from the Qinghai Provincial Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs that the latest monitoring results show that Qinghai Lake's bare carp resources have increased by 0.71 million tons this year compared with the previous year, reaching 108,500 tons, compared with the initial protection in 2002, a cumulative increase of more than 40 times.
Qinghai Lake's naked carp commonly known as â€œtrouppyâ€ â€œtroundfishâ€ is a unique precious fish species in Qinghai Lake, which plays a pivotal role in maintaining the safety and biodiversity of the ecological chain of â€œwater-fish-birdâ€ in the Qinghai Lake basin.
In the 1960s and 1970s, affected by factors such as the increasing environmental degradation of man-made hunting and naked carp breeding waters, the number of naked carp in Qinghai Lake plummeted, and the amount of naked carp resources in Qinghai Lake was only 2,592 tons in 2002.
In 2004, in the Red List of Chinese Species, Qinghai Lake naked carp was listed as an endangered species.
Since 2003, Qinghai Province has implemented the implementation of lake fish breeding, prohibiting any units, collectives and individuals from fishing naked carp to the main rivers and tributaries of Qinghai Lake and the lake area, and prohibiting the sale of naked carp and its products.
At the same time, through the artificial proliferation and release and the cleaning of Qinghai Lake's main rivers and rivers, the design of a scientific and reasonable "fish channel" and other measures to continue to increase protection efforts, Qinghai Lake's bare carp resources have increased year by year.
Yang Lin, deputy director of the Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of Qinghai Province, introduced that as of now, Qinghai Lake naked carp has accumulatively implemented nearly 180 million tails of artificial proliferation and release, contributing more than 23% to the recovery of Qinghai Lake's bare carp resources.
Qinghai Sanjiangyuan area is an important ecological barrier and water conservation area in China and even Asia, and Qinghai Lake is a natural barrier and ecological functional area to control the spread of desertification in the west to the east.
In order to protect the ecological environment and protect aquatic wildlife in the Sanjiangyuan area and the waters of Qinghai Lake and maintain the biodiversity of the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau, since this year, Qinghai has successively issued notices on the ban on fishing in the key waters of the Yangtze River, the Yellow River and Qinghai Lake, and built a "one river, one river, one lake" comprehensive no-catch management system.
