Yunnan: Co-ordinating the management of public welfare posts in rural areas - Xinhua.com
Xinhua News Agency, Kunming, December 12 (Reporter Lin Bifeng) In order to continue to do a good job in the employment assistance of people out of poverty and consolidate and expand the achievements of poverty alleviation, Yunnan Province has recently introduced policies to promote the revitalization of rural public welfare post management, helping to comprehensively promote rural revitalization.
According to the relevant person in charge of the Yunnan Provincial Human Resources and Social Affairs Department, at present, Yunnan has developed a total of 448,300 rural public welfare positions, which are used to place the employment of rural difficult groups such as poverty-stricken laborers, which play an important role in helping the people out of poverty to achieve employment income, consolidating the achievements of poverty alleviation, and effectively improving the ability of rural public services.
The new regulations are jointly issued by seven departments such as Yunnan people's society, rural revitalization, and finance, and mainly unify the target scope, fund management, job development, and job management for grass-roots recruitment of rural public welfare positions.
In terms of job development, the new regulations are clear, in accordance with the principles of "on-the-dose, on-the-shelf, dynamic management, total control", "who develops, who uses, who is responsible", and "one person, one post, voluntary disclosure, and unified management".
The recruitment process must be carried out in accordance with announcements, declarations, audits, publicity, recruitment, pre-post training, and arrangements.
In addition, the new regulations also clarify the specific responsibilities of the main development departments of rural public welfare posts, subsidy standards and subsidy methods for rural public welfare positions, and stipulate that the development departments of rural public welfare posts should purchase commercial insurance for rural public welfare posts; the relevant departments are required to supervise the issuance of subsidies for rural public welfare posts on a regular basis.
