In Mauritius and other countries for the first time to find cases of Omikjon virus infection - Xinhua
BEIJING, Dec. 12 (Xinhua) -- Mauritius, Cyprus and Malawi recently reported for the first time the discovery of cases of the new coronavirus Omikron strain.
For the first time on the 10th, Mauritius has reported two cases of Omikjon virus infection in the country.
According to the Minister of Health of the Mao, Kailesh Jagutpal, one infected person was a tourist who arrived in Mauritius from South Africa on 27 November; the other infected person was a Mauritian resident, who tested positive for nucleic acid on November 30 after contact with a person who had recently returned to South Africa.
After the isolation treatment by the hospital, the nucleic acid test results of these two infected people have turned negative, and they have now returned to their respective places of residence.
The Ministry of Health of Cyprus announced on the 10th that it has confirmed three cases of Omikjon virus infection for the first time in the country.
All three were students who had returned from traveling abroad at the beginning of this month and had not been admitted to the hospital for treatment due to being mild.
In order to prevent the spread of the Omikron strain, the Cypriot government has continuously increased its prevention and control efforts.
From December 6th to January 10 next year, passengers over the age of 12 entering by plane will be required to undergo nucleic acid testing at the airport at their own expense.
On the 10th, the Ministry of Health also announced that it will start vaccinating children between the ages of 5 and 11 in the country with the Pfizer new crown vaccine
Malawi's health minister, Kumpitzer Chipunda, said on the 9th that for the first time in the country, three cases of infection with the Omikjung strain have been found in the country.
The country’s health department sequenced the genomes of 12 new coronavirus-positive samples collected from Nov. 9 to Dec. 2 and found three cases of infection.
