The starry strace has about the Geminid meteor shower ushered in on the 14th - Xinhua Net
Xinhua News Agency, Tianjin, December 12 (Reporter Zhou Runjian) astronomical science experts introduced that as the last large-scale meteor shower of the year, one of the three major meteor showers in the northern hemisphere will usher in the Geminid meteor shower on December 14, and friends who like the meteor shower can make observations in the middle of the night.
The Geminid meteor shower photographed by Beijing astronomy enthusiasts in Qinghai on December 13, 2018.
Most of the parent object of the meteor shower is the periodic comet, but the parent object of the Geminoid meteor shower is the asteroid 3200, which is an Apollo-type asteroid.
The Geminid meteor shower is also currently known to be the 2nd meteor shower that is not "bred" by comets.
Xiu Lipeng, director of the Tianjin Astronomical Society and an expert in astronomical science, said that just like New Year's blockbusters, Geminid meteor showers generally appear at the end of the year, and the "release schedule" can last from December 4th to 17th.
The meteor shower is known for its large flow and stability, and together with the quadrant meteor shower and Perseid meteor shower, it is known as the three major meteor showers in the Northern Hemisphere.
A distinctive feature of the Geminid meteor shower is the slowness of the meteoroid, the richness of the color, and the large number of fire meteors, which is suitable for both visual and astrophotographic beginners.
The Geminid meteor shower photographed by Tianjin astronomy enthusiast Yang Jing on December 13, 2020 in Jizhou, Tianjin.
Astronomical forecasts show that this year's Geminid meteor shower will usher in about 15:00 on December 14, when ZHR (under ideal observation conditions, when the radiation point is directly above the top of the head, the number of meteors can be seen per hour) is 150.
Geminid meteor shower recommended index map.
"Last year, the Geminid meteor shower was impressed, but this year's Geminid meteor shower will be disturbed by moonlight, and the wonderful degree will be a little discount.
On the 14th, for the 11th of the lunar calendar, the moon phase is the convex moon, and the bright moonlight will interfere with the observation, but the moon will fall in the middle of the night, and at this time the radiation point of the Geminid meteor shower will rise relatively high.
Friends who like the meteor shower can observe these few hours behind in the middle of the middle of the month, but pay attention to the cold and keep warm."
How can we see as many meteors as possible?
"It is not recommended to make observations in the city, you can choose a high-altitude, low-light, north-east-facing field of view in the suburbs or villages, and then patiently wait until the moon falls, visual observation."
It should be noted that the Geminid meteor shower flows in all directions are very large, and there is no need to stare at the radiation point of the Geminid meteor shower all the time when observing.
Friends who like photography want to shoot a gorgeous 'shooter shower blockbuster', it's best to choose a wide-angle, large aperture lens, using a high ISO and maximum aperture when shooting.
Based on terms of stability and continuity, tripods, spare batteries and shutter lines are also essential.”
Pupeng reminded him.
What is the difference between laser TV and traditional TV in terms of market positioning?
With my understanding, the traditional TV mentioned by the subject should refer to the LCD TV, and the difference between the laser TV and LCD TV in terms of market positioning, there are mainly the following two points:
First of all, the laser TV is more focused on the large screen market.
Compared with the market positioning of the LCD TV, the laser TV is obviously more focused on the large screen market, or the laser TV itself is the product of the big screen.
At present, the size of the mainstream LCD TV is more than 55 inches to 65 inches, and the size of the laser TV is generally more than 75 inches, and the largest is more than 100 inches, which fully meets the needs of users for large-screen color TVs.
In recent years, laser TV shipments and sales accounted for an increasing proportion in the world, accounting for more than 60% of the overall TV sales of 80 inches and above.
According to the forecast of Zhongyikang, in 2020, the sales growth of the laser TV market will exceed 140%, and it will continue to maintain rapid growth.
The reason why it has such good results in the large-screen market is mainly due to the excellent performance of laser TV in eye protection.
Based on the imaging principle of laser TV diffuse reflection, the light emitted by the laser light source is not directly transmitted into the eyeball, compared to the backlight of the LCD TV, the imaging process is closer to the imaging process of objects under natural conditions, and the irritation to the eyes is also smaller.
China Electronics Technology Standardization Research Institute Saisi Laboratory and Beijing Union Hospital ophthalmology experts, through the same conditions under the same conditions to watch the laser TV and LCD TV rigorous comparison test, arrived at 144 sets of test data.
The data confirms that laser TV does have strong eye protection characteristics, and even has a certain improvement effect in specific aspects.
At the moment when vision health is receiving more and more attention, laser TV not only attracts more and more users by virtue of eye protection advantages, but also opens another breakthrough in the color TV market.
Second, laser TV is more focused on the high-end market.
Contrary to the continuous decline in the price of LCD TVs, most of the prices of commercially available laser TVs are more than 10,000 yuan, and with the upgrading of size and light sources, the prices have gradually risen.
Why are laser TVs so expensive?
It certainly makes sense.
Under the continuous development of light sources and technical levels, laser TVs have many advantages that can not be achieved with LCD TVs and projections.
With the ultra-short focal length projection technology, the projection distance of the laser TV is shorter than that of traditional projection equipment, which can achieve a 100-inch large-screen experience in a short distance, the required space is not large, and the host is small and occupies a very small place.
In terms of brightness, large brand laser TVs can reach more than 2,000 lumens.
Coupled with lower heat, small loss of equipment, the service life of the TV is also longer.
In addition, many high-end laser TV models are also equipped with many cutting-edge technologies such as true 4K ultra-high-definition image quality, artificial intelligence systems, and bionic screens, which can bring more shocking audio-visual experiences to users.
Talking about false demand, but the product of demand subdivision, on picture quality and input-output ratio, laser TV is not a video player's dish, want to take into account the large screen and the viewing environment is insufficient, you can try, everything is pros and cons, after weighing their own judgment, you are afraid to listen to the words.
Simply put, the ultra wide-angle near-focus projector - laser TV, in order to be close to the curtain, had to use expensive ultra-wide-angle lenses and mirrors, which does not conform to the best optical design.
In order to shield part of the ambient light, the use of microstructure of the Fignel curtain, the cost is high, the price of 80 inches can basically replace a 65-inch liquid crystal.
There is also a point, I especially hate projection manufacturers take diffuse reflection on the eyes of this kind of selling point, please, the eyes can see the light on the screen for the eyes is direct light, you diffuse to the ceiling, the eyes can not be seen, the real LCD TV is also diffuse "straight shot", open the TV ceiling is not also illuminated?
In addition, if the projection screen is not a diffuse reflection, it will not become an appearance at all.
It is precisely ignored that the hot spot (light spot) effect of the high-gain curtain is ignored, and a large amount of light is reflected to the eyes at a certain angle, which is really uncomfortable.
