Sino-Vietnamese army "peace rescue - 2021" joint exercise successfully concluded - Xinhua
HANOI, Dec. 12 (Xinhua) -- On the morning of the 12th, all the Chinese participating detachments that participated in the Sino-Vietnamese army's "Peace Rescue-2021" joint exercise were safely returned to China's Guangxi territory, marking the successful completion of this seven-day training mission.
In this joint exercise, the Sino-Vietnamese army focused on the major issue of humanitarian medical rescue, closely adhered to the mission mission of health service to save lives and help injuries, and completed the contents of the joint health service command, joint on-site rescue, and mass disposal of the wounded in accordance with the actual combat standards, effectively improving the security guarantee capabilities of the two militaries.
The results of the exercise have been affirmed by the two militaries.
At the closing ceremony of the exercise, the director of the steering committee of the Vietnamese exercise, the deputy director and chief of staff of the General Logistics Department of the Vietnamese People's Army, Nguyen Xiong Sheng, said that through this exercise, Vietnamese military doctors have learned the knowledge of the organization and professional activities of the exercise from Chinese military doctors, as well as China's medical and security equipment.
The results of the exercise proved the professional ability of the military medical forces of the two countries in medical assistance and epidemic prevention and control.
Chen Chunming, leader of China's steering and coordination group and deputy director of the health department of the logistics support department of the Central Military Commission, said that the exercise is another pioneering and innovative practice on the basis of the successful holding of joint clinics in 2018, which is a very important milestone.
During the exercise, the Chinese People's Liberation Army donated medical protective masks, medical protective clothing, rapid nucleic acid testing instruments and other health and epidemic prevention materials to the Vietnamese People's Army.
